{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"augmented reality augmented reality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md","fileName":"Augmented Reality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Augmented Reality","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[XR Environments]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Environments","3D Tracking","Mixed Reality","3D User Interface","Spatial Registration","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"augmented reality augmented reality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md","fileName":"Augmented Reality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Augmented Reality","heading":"Augmented Reality","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Augmented reality is an approach that uses displays, [[3D Tracking]], and other technologies to enhance a user's view of the real environment with synthetic objects or information.\n\nAR design must account for both physical and virtual content. Display limits, changing lighting, inaccurate registration, and occlusion can make virtual information hard to interpret. Interaction should make it clear how real and virtual objects relate, while controls should avoid hiding important parts of the environment.\n\nAR is part of the broader [[Mixed Reality]] continuum and uses a [[3D User Interface]] when tasks occur directly in a three-dimensional spatial context.\n\nAn AR system combines real and virtual information, updates interactively in real time, and keeps corresponding information [[Spatial Registration|registered in three dimensions]]. These requirements do not prescribe a visual or head-worn device: spatial audio or haptic augmentation can also connect information to the physical environment. A working system coordinates tracking, registration, visualization, and a model that relates real and virtual entities.","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Environments","3D Tracking","Mixed Reality","3D User Interface","Spatial Registration","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"augmented reality augmented reality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Augmented Reality.md","fileName":"Augmented Reality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Augmented Reality","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[augmentedreality_pearson.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Environments","3D Tracking","Mixed Reality","3D User Interface","Spatial Registration","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}